# PndPidCorrelator

## TL;DR
### Minimal working example
```c++
PndMasterRunAna *fRun = new PndMasterRunAna();
FairGeane *Geane = new FairGeane(); // need Geane for default version
fRun->AddTask(Geane);

// default version of PndPidCorrelator uses default detector setup
PndPidCorrelator *corr = new PndPidCorrelator();
// set track branch in barrel spectromenter
corr->SetBarrelTrackBranch("SttMvdGemGenTrack");
// set track branch in forward spectromenter
corr->SetForwardTrackBranch("FtsIdealGenTrack");

fRun->AddTask(corr);
```

### Setting detectors manually
Create a setup in which only calorimeter, DRC, track, MVD and STT pid information is read out.

```c++
PndMasterRunAna *fRun = new PndMasterRunAna();

// disable default setup
PndPidCorrelator *corr = new PndPidCorrelator(kFALSE);
// set track branch in barrel spectromenter
corr->SetBarrelTrackBranch("SttMvdGemGenTrack");
// set track branch in forward spectromenter
corr->SetForwardTrackBranch("FtsIdealGenTrack");

// set DetectorInfo classes to be used: PndPidCalorimeterInfo and PndPidDrcInfo
corr->SetCalorimeterInfo(new PndPidCalorimeterInfo());
corr->SetDrcInfo(new PndPidDrcInfo());

// set TrackingInfo -> disable default and set tracking detectors manually
corr->SetTrackingInfo(new PndPidTrackingInfo(kFALSE)); // track (pid) info is used
corr->SetMvdInfo(new PndPidMvdInfo()); // use MVD pid info
corr->SetSttInfo(new PndPidSttInfo()); // use STT pid info

fRun->AddTask(corr);
```

## General
The **PndPidCorrelator** gathers pid information from different detectors of the PANDA setup. Its task is to correlate tracks and detector hits and to create [PndPidCandidates](../../pnddata/PidData/PndPidCandidate.h) containing the information of all detector hits correlated to the same track. 
In doing so, the **PndPidCorrelator** is able to classify **PidCandidates** into charged and neutral candidates. The latter will be created in case a hit in the EMC/FSC setup is measured but no track can be correlated to this hit.

As the rules for correlating hits and tracks are different for each detector, **DetectorInfo** classes containing  the logic for a certain detector are plugged into the **PidCorrelator**. The **PidCorrelator** itself doesn't care about the exact implementations of these DetectorInfo classes, it only organizes them.

## DetectorInfo classes
There are **DetectorInfo** classes for each detector of the PANDA setup. They are derived from the **PndPidDetectorInfo** class defined in [PndPidDetectorInfo.h](PndPidDetectorInfo.h) and sorted into **PidDetectors** and **TrackingDetectors** (see list below). 
The **DetectorInfo** classes contain all the necessary logic to correlate a given track to hits in the detector they're concerned with.

### PidDetectors
- [PndPidCalorimeterInfo](PidDetectors/PndPidCalorimeterInfo.h)
- [PndPidDrcInfo](PidDetectors/PndPidDrcInfo.h)
- [PndPidDskInfo](PidDetectors/PndPidDskInfo.h)
- [PndPidRichInfo](PidDetectors/PndPidRichInfo.h)
- [PndPidTofInfo](PidDetectors/PndPidTofInfo.h)
- [PndPidFtofInfo](PidDetectors/PndPidFtofInfo.h)
- [PndPidMdtInfo](PidDetectors/PndPidMdtInfo.h)
- [PndPidFmdtInfo](PidDetectors/PndPidFmdtInfo.h)

### TrackingDetectors
- [PndPidMvdInfo](TrackingDetectors/PndPidMvdInfo.h)
- [PndPidGemInfo](TrackingDetectors/PndPidGemInfo.h)
- [PndPidSttInfo](TrackingDetectors/PndPidSttInfo.h)
- [PndPidFtsInfo](TrackingDetectors/PndPidFtsInfo.h)

